  "question": {
    "text": "A source of sound is moving with a velocity of <math><mn>50</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> towards a stationary observer. The observer measures the frequency of sound as <math><mn>500</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></math>. The apparent frequency of sound as heard by the observer when source is moving away from him with the same speed is (Speed of sound at room temperature is <math><mn>350</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>400</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>Hz</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>600</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>Hz</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>375</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>Hz</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>175.5</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>Hz</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Speed of sound, <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>350&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Velocity of sound, <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />From Doppler's principle,<br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msup></math> case, <math><mi>f</mi><mi>′</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math> ......(i)<br /><br /><math><mn>500</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>350</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>350</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math><br /><br />Where, <math><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo></math> frequency of the source<br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msup></math> case, <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>'</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>'</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>350</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>350</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math> ....(ii)<br /><br />From equation (i) and (ii) we get<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>'</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>500</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>350</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>350</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>300</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>'</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>375</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>Hz</mi><mi></mi></math>"
  }
}